I have a complete picture. Here is my report.

## Summary

All owner identity / duplicate-detection logic lives in **two** files — the `Owner` entity (static helpers) and `OwnerRestControllerV1` (the intake pipeline). There is **no separate service class** for this logic; `ClinicService` is only used for persistence/lookup. Critically, I found a **spec/implementation mismatch**: the acceptance test expects a SHA-256/soundex-based "v2" identity key that the code does **not** implement (see section 8).

---

### 1. identityKey / identity hash computation

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`**

